{"abstract":[{"text":"Write the rules of a simulation as systems, and let their parameters state what they read and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"write.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/declaringsystems"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A system is a type with a "},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method that a schedule calls once per run. The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"macro turns a structure into a system from the parameters of its "},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method. Each parameter’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type says what part of the world the system works on and whether it reads or writes it, so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is always exact, and a schedule can run systems that don’t conflict at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same time."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Read and Write Components","level":3,"anchor":"Read-and-Write-Components"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Take a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query"},{"text":" to read components, and iterate it as you would a world’s query","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"results. Take an ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update"},{"text":" to change them in place. An","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"update can also read other components with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Over"},{"text":", and narrow the entities it visits with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Where"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@System","struct Climb {","    func run(_ climbers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        climbers { position, row in","            position.y += abs(row.components.dy)","        }","    }","}","","var world = World()","let climber = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 0, dy: -3))","let statue = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 0, dy: -3), Frozen())","Schedule { Climb() }.run(on: &world)","","print(world[Position.self, of: climber].y)","\/\/ Prints \"3.0\"","print(world[Position.self, of: statue].y)","\/\/ Prints \"0.0\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Climb"},{"type":"text","text":" writes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"type":"text","text":" and reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Velocity"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Frozen"},{"type":"text","text":". It conflicts with any system that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Velocity"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Frozen"},{"type":"text","text":", or reads or writes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"type":"text","text":", and runs at the same time as any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A parameter’s filter is a list of filter types in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Where","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/With"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Without"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Added"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Changed"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Allows"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/AnyOf"},{"text":" of filter types. Each mirrors the query filter","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the same name.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two parameters that name the same component, one of them writing it, are a compile-time error."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A conflict the macro can’t see by name, such as one through a type alias, traps when a schedule"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"takes the system."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Read and Write Resources and Events","level":3,"anchor":"Read-and-Write-Resources-and-Events"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" reads a resource and a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" changes one. An ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sends events, and an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" reads the events sent since the system last read them. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"following schedule sends a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Damage","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" event for each entity below the ground, then applies the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"damage to its target’s health:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let knight = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: -1), Health(current: 30))","","let frame = Schedule {","    UpdateEvents()","    Combat()","    ApplyDamage().after(Combat.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","print(world[Health.self, of: knight].current)","\/\/ Prints \"20\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" declares "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Combat"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader"},{"type":"text","text":" declares "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplyDamage"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Spawn and Despawn Entities","level":3,"anchor":"Spawn-and-Despawn-Entities"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that runs alongside others can’t spawn or despawn entities directly, because that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changes every component type at once. Take an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instead, and queue"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the changes. Commands apply at the end of the wave the system runs in, so systems ordered after"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it see them:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@System","struct RemoveDefeated {","    func run(_ fighters: Query<Health>, _ commands: inout Commands) {","        for (entity, health) in fighters where health.current <= 0 {","            commands.despawn(entity)","        }","    }","}","","var world = World()","let knight = world.spawn(Health(current: 0))","world.spawn(Health(current: 12))","Schedule { RemoveDefeated() }.run(on: &world)","","print(world.contains(knight))","\/\/ Prints \"false\"","print(world.count)","\/\/ Prints \"1\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A commands parameter conflicts with nothing, so it doesn’t stop a system from running at the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same time as others.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Take the Whole World","level":3,"anchor":"Take-the-Whole-World"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method that takes ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout World","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" makes a system that can change anything. Its access is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a schedule runs it alone, after the systems written before it and before those written","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"after it. Use one for work that touches many types at once, such as loading a level.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To write a system by hand instead of with the macro, conform a type to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", implement"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and declare an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" listing every type the system reads and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writes."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Run on the Main Actor","level":3,"anchor":"Run-on-the-Main-Actor"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mark a system type, or its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":" to make a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem"},{"type":"text","text":", which a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"schedule runs on the main actor after the other systems of its wave. Use one to carry results"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the world to a user interface."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once you’ve declared systems, see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to order them and run them only when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a condition holds."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"],"anchor":"Essentials","generated":true}],"metadata":{"title":"Declaring Systems","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Declaring Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem"],"anchor":"Declaring-Systems"},{"title":"System Parameters","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents"],"anchor":"System-Parameters"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventWriter":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that sends events of one type."}],"role":"symbol","title":"EventWriter","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/eventwriter","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EventWriter"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EventWriter"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/RemovedComponents":{"abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that lists the entities that lost a component since the system last read","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"RemovedComponents","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/removedcomponents","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RemovedComponents","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RemovedComponents","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Added":{"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/added","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Added","role":"symbol","title":"Added","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Added","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Added","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A filter type that passes the entities whose component of type "},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" was added since the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"world’s last run."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/run(in:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Runs the system’s rule once on a world.","type":"text"}],"title":"run(in:)","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/run(in:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)","required":true,"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"run","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"in","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceReader":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that reads a resource."}],"role":"symbol","title":"ResourceReader","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcereader","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceReader"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceReader"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Hold a world in your app or game engine, feed it each frame’s input, and let the objects outside"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it read results and take part in a step."}],"title":"Driving a World from an App","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/drivingaworldfromanapp","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/MainActorSystem":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that runs on the main actor, for work that touches main-actor state such as a user"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interface."}],"role":"symbol","title":"MainActorSystem","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/mainactorsystem","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MainActorSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MainActorSystem","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Without":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/without","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Without","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Without","title":"Without","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Without","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A filter type that passes the entities holding no component of type ","type":"text"},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventReader":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that reads the events of one type sent since the system last read them."}],"role":"symbol","title":"EventReader","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/eventreader","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Update":{"abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that changes a component of every entity that holds it.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Update","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/update","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Update"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Update"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SchedulingSystems":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Order the systems of a schedule, run them only when a condition holds, and find out how a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schedule runs them.","type":"text"}],"title":"Scheduling Systems","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedulingsystems","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems","role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/With":{"abstract":[{"text":"A filter type that passes the entities holding a component of type ","type":"text"},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"With","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/With","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/with","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"With"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"With"}]},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Query":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A description of the entities to visit and the components to read from each."}],"role":"symbol","title":"Query","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/query","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Query"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Query"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"title":"Systems","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceWriter":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that reads and writes a resource.","type":"text"}],"title":"ResourceWriter","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcewriter","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceWriter"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceWriter"}]},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Changed":{"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/changed","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Changed","role":"symbol","title":"Changed","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Changed","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Changed","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A filter type that passes the entities whose component of type ","type":"text"},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" was added or changed since","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the world’s last run.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Allows":{"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/allows","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Allows","role":"symbol","title":"Allows","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Allows","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Allows","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A filter type that also passes the entities holding a disabling component of type ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"C"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/AnyOf":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/anyof","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/AnyOf","role":"symbol","title":"AnyOf","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AnyOf"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AnyOf"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A group of types an entity matches by matching at least one of them.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System":{"abstract":[{"text":"A rule that reads and changes a world, run once each time its schedule runs.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"System","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/access":{"defaultImplementations":1,"kind":"symbol","title":"access","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/access","type":"topic","role":"symbol","required":true,"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"access","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Access","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6AccessV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","abstract":[{"text":"The component, resource and event types the system reads and writes, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if it may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change anything.","type":"text"}]},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Commands":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A buffer of changes to a world, recorded now and applied later in the order they were","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"recorded.","type":"text"}],"title":"Commands","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/commands","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Commands"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Commands"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Makes a type a system whose access comes from the parameters of its "},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method."}],"role":"symbol","title":"System()","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"macro"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}]}}}